  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>golimumab</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L04AB06</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Lee JB et al. 2023</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>children and young adults with type 1 diabetes</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>golimumab</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_golimumab/Golimumab_Lee2023_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>apparent clearance</td><td>0.85</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>CL/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>apparent volume of distribution</td><td>16.0</td><td>L</td><td><small>V/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>absorption rate constant</td><td>1.01</td><td>/day</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr></table><h4>About golimumab</h4><p>Golimumab is a monoclonal antibody that blocks tumour necrosis factor alpha and is used to treat inflammatory conditions such as rheumatoid and psoriatic arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, and ulcerative colitis. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union, and is widely used for these immune-mediated diseases.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q413879\">Wikidata Q413879</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Golimumab\">Golimumab</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Lee JB et al. (2023). Population Pharmacokinetics and Exposure-Response Modeling Analyses of Golimumab in Children and Young Adults With Recently Diagnosed Type 1 Diabetes. <i>Journal of clinical pharmacology 63(6):721–731</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcph.2217\">10.1002/jcph.2217</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36854991\">36854991</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Lee_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
